#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:301
msgid ""
"Setuptools no longer accepts options containing uppercase or dash characters "
"in ``setup.cfg``. Please ensure to write the options in ``setup.cfg`` using "
"the :wiki:`lower_snake_case <Snake_case>` convention (e.g. ``Name => name``, "
"``install-requires => install_requires``). This is a follow-up on "
"deprecations introduced in `v54.1.0 <https://setuptools.pypa.io/en/latest/"
"history.html#v54-1-0>`_ (see `#1608 <https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/"
"issues/1608>`_) and `v54.1.1 <https://setuptools.pypa.io/en/latest/history."
"html#v54-1-1>`_ (see `#2592 <https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/"
"issues/2592>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:309
msgid ""
"This change *does not affect configurations in* ``pyproject.toml`` (which "
"uses the :wiki:`lower-kebab-case <Letter_case#Kebab_case>` convention "
"following the precedent set in :pep:`517`/:pep:`518`). (`#4870 <https://"
"github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/4870>`_)"
msgstr ""

