#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7784
msgid "``ftp:`` download URLs now work correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7786
msgid ""
"The default ``--index-url`` is now ``https://pypi.python.org/simple``, to "
"use the Python Package Index's new simpler (and faster!) REST API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7790
msgid "0.6c6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7792
msgid ""
"Added ``--egg-path`` option to ``develop`` command, allowing you to force ``."
"egg-link`` files to use relative paths (allowing them to be shared across "
"platforms on a networked drive)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7796
msgid "Fix not building binary RPMs correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7798
msgid ""
"Fix \"eggsecutables\" (such as setuptools' own egg) only being runnable with "
"bash-compatible shells."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7801
msgid ""
"Fix ``#!`` parsing problems in Windows ``.exe`` script wrappers, when there "
"was whitespace inside a quoted argument or at the end of the ``#!`` line (a "
"regression introduced in 0.6c4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7805
msgid ""
"Fix ``test`` command possibly failing if an older version of the project "
"being tested was installed on ``sys.path`` ahead of the test source "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7809
msgid ""
"Fix ``find_packages()`` treating ``ez_setup`` and directories with ``.`` in "
"their names as packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7812
msgid ""
"EasyInstall no longer aborts the installation process if a URL it wants to "
"retrieve can't be downloaded, unless the URL is an actual package download. "
"Instead, it issues a warning and tries to keep going."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7816
msgid ""
"Fixed distutils-style scripts originally built on Windows having their line "
"endings doubled when installed on any platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7819
msgid ""
"Added ``--local-snapshots-ok`` flag, to allow building eggs from projects "
"installed using ``setup.py develop``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7822
msgid "Fixed not HTML-decoding URLs scraped from web pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7825
msgid "0.6c5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7827
msgid ""
"Fix uploaded ``bdist_rpm`` packages being described as ``bdist_egg`` "
"packages under Python versions less than 2.5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7830
msgid ""
"Fix uploaded ``bdist_wininst`` packages being described as suitable for "
"\"any\" version by Python 2.5, even if a ``--target-version`` was specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7833
msgid ""
"Fixed ``.dll`` files on Cygwin not having executable permissions when an egg "
"is installed unzipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7837
msgid "0.6c4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7839
msgid ""
"Overhauled Windows script wrapping to support ``bdist_wininst`` better. "
"Scripts installed with ``bdist_wininst`` will always use ``#!python.exe`` or "
"``#!pythonw.exe`` as the executable name (even when built on non-Windows "
"platforms!), and the wrappers will look for the executable in the script's "
"parent directory (which should find the right version of Python)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7845
msgid ""
"Fix ``upload`` command not uploading files built by ``bdist_rpm`` or "
"``bdist_wininst`` under Python 2.3 and 2.4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7848
msgid ""
"Add support for \"eggsecutable\" headers: a ``#!/bin/sh`` script that is "
"prepended to an ``.egg`` file to allow it to be run as a script on Unix-ish "
"platforms.  (This is mainly so that setuptools itself can have a single-file "
"installer on Unix, without doing multiple downloads, dealing with firewalls, "
"etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7854
msgid ""
"Fix problem with empty revision numbers in Subversion 1.4 ``entries`` files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7856
msgid ""
"Use cross-platform relative paths in ``easy-install.pth`` when doing "
"``develop`` and the source directory is a subdirectory of the installation "
"target directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7860
msgid ""
"Fix a problem installing eggs with a system packaging tool if the project "
"contained an implicit namespace package; for example if the ``setup()`` "
"listed a namespace package ``foo.bar`` without explicitly listing ``foo`` as "
"a namespace package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7865
msgid ""
"Added support for HTTP \"Basic\" authentication using ``http://user:"
"pass@host`` URLs.  If a password-protected page contains links to the same "
"host (and protocol), those links will inherit the credentials used to access "
"the original page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7870
msgid ""
"Removed all special support for Sourceforge mirrors, as Sourceforge's mirror "
"system now works well for non-browser downloads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7873
msgid ""
"Fixed not recognizing ``win32.exe`` installers that included a custom bitmap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7876
msgid ""
"Fixed not allowing ``os.open()`` of paths outside the sandbox, even if they "
"are opened read-only (e.g. reading ``/dev/urandom`` for random numbers, as "
"is done by ``os.urandom()`` on some platforms)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7880
msgid ""
"Fixed a problem with ``.pth`` testing on Windows when ``sys.executable`` has "
"a space in it (e.g., the user installed Python to a ``Program Files`` "
"directory)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7885
msgid "0.6c3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7887
msgid "Fixed breakages caused by Subversion 1.4's new \"working copy\" format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7889
msgid ""
"You can once again use \"python -m easy_install\" with Python 2.4 and above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7891
msgid "Python 2.5 compatibility fixes added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7894
msgid "0.6c2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7896
msgid ""
"The ``ez_setup`` module displays the conflicting version of setuptools (and "
"its installation location) when a script requests a version that's not "
"available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7900
msgid ""
"Running ``setup.py develop`` on a setuptools-using project will now install "
"setuptools if needed, instead of only downloading the egg."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7903
msgid ""
"Windows script wrappers now support quoted arguments and arguments "
"containing spaces.  (Patch contributed by Jim Fulton.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7906
msgid ""
"The ``ez_setup.py`` script now actually works when you put a setuptools ``."
"egg`` alongside it for bootstrapping an offline machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7909
msgid ""
"A writable installation directory on ``sys.path`` is no longer required to "
"download and extract a source distribution using ``--editable``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7912
msgid ""
"Generated scripts now use ``-x`` on the ``#!`` line when ``sys.executable`` "
"contains non-ASCII characters, to prevent deprecation warnings about an "
"unspecified encoding when the script is run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7917
msgid "0.6c1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7919
msgid ""
"Fixed ``AttributeError`` when trying to download a ``setup_requires`` "
"dependency when a distribution lacks a ``dependency_links`` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7922
msgid ""
"Made ``zip-safe`` and ``not-zip-safe`` flag files contain a single byte, so "
"as to play better with packaging tools that complain about zero-length files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7926
msgid ""
"Made ``setup.py develop`` respect the ``--no-deps`` option, which it "
"previously was ignoring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7929
msgid ""
"Support ``extra_path`` option to ``setup()`` when ``install`` is run in "
"backward-compatibility mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7932
msgid ""
"Source distributions now always include a ``setup.cfg`` file that explicitly "
"sets ``egg_info`` options such that they produce an identical version number "
"to the source distribution's version number.  (Previously, the default "
"version number could be different due to the use of ``--tag-date``, or if "
"the version was overridden on the command line that built the source "
"distribution.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7939
msgid ""
"EasyInstall now includes setuptools version information in the ``User-"
"Agent`` string sent to websites it visits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7943
msgid "0.6b4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7945
msgid ""
"Fix ``register`` not obeying name/version set by ``egg_info`` command, if "
"``egg_info`` wasn't explicitly run first on the same command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7948
msgid ""
"Added ``--no-date`` and ``--no-svn-revision`` options to ``egg_info`` "
"command, to allow suppressing tags configured in ``setup.cfg``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7951
msgid ""
"Fixed redundant warnings about missing ``README`` file(s); it should now "
"appear only if you are actually a source distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7954
msgid "Fix creating Python wrappers for non-Python scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7956
msgid ""
"Fix ``ftp://`` directory listing URLs from causing a crash when used in the "
"\"Home page\" or \"Download URL\" slots on PyPI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7959
msgid ""
"Fix ``sys.path_importer_cache`` not being updated when an existing zipfile "
"or directory is deleted/overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7962
msgid "Fix not recognizing HTML 404 pages from package indexes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7964
msgid ""
"Allow ``file://`` URLs to be used as a package index.  URLs that refer to "
"directories will use an internally-generated directory listing if there is "
"no ``index.html`` file in the directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7968
msgid ""
"Allow external links in a package index to be specified using "
"``rel=\"homepage\"`` or ``rel=\"download\"``, without needing the old PyPI-"
"specific visible markup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7972
msgid ""
"Suppressed warning message about possibly-misspelled project name, if an egg "
"or link for that project name has already been seen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7976
msgid "0.6b3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7978
msgid ""
"Fix ``bdist_egg`` not including files in subdirectories of ``.egg-info``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7980
msgid ""
"Allow ``.py`` files found by the ``include_package_data`` option to be "
"automatically included. Remove duplicate data file matches if both "
"``include_package_data`` and ``package_data`` are used to refer to the same "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7985
msgid ""
"Fix local ``--find-links`` eggs not being copied except with ``--always-"
"copy``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7988
msgid ""
"Fix sometimes not detecting local packages installed outside of \"site\" "
"directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7991
msgid ""
"Fix mysterious errors during initial ``setuptools`` install, caused by "
"``ez_setup`` trying to run ``easy_install`` twice, due to a code fallthru "
"after deleting the egg from which it's running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7996
msgid "0.6b2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:7998
msgid ""
"Don't install or update a ``site.py`` patch when installing to a "
"``PYTHONPATH`` directory with ``--multi-version``, unless an ``easy-install."
"pth`` file is already in use there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8002
msgid ""
"Construct ``.pth`` file paths in such a way that installing an egg whose "
"name begins with ``import`` doesn't cause a syntax error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8005
msgid ""
"Fixed a bogus warning message that wasn't updated since the 0.5 versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8008
msgid "0.6b1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8010
msgid ""
"Strip ``module`` from the end of compiled extension modules when computing "
"the name of a ``.py`` loader/wrapper.  (Python's import machinery ignores "
"this suffix when searching for an extension module.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8014
msgid ""
"Better ambiguity management: accept ``#egg`` name/version even if processing "
"what appears to be a correctly-named distutils file, and ignore ``.egg`` "
"files with no ``-``, since valid Python ``.egg`` files always have a version "
"number (but Scheme eggs often don't)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8019
msgid ""
"Support ``file://`` links to directories in ``--find-links``, so that "
"easy_install can build packages from local source checkouts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8022
msgid ""
"Added automatic retry for Sourceforge mirrors.  The new download process is "
"to first just try dl.sourceforge.net, then randomly select mirror IPs and "
"remove ones that fail, until something works.  The removed IPs stay removed "
"for the remainder of the run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8027
msgid "Ignore bdist_dumb distributions when looking at download URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8030
msgid "0.6a11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8032
msgid "Added ``test_loader`` keyword to support custom test loaders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8034
msgid ""
"Added ``setuptools.file_finders`` entry point group to allow implementing "
"revision control plugins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8037
msgid "Added ``--identity`` option to ``upload`` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8039
msgid ""
"Added ``dependency_links`` to allow specifying URLs for ``--find-links``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8041
msgid ""
"Enhanced test loader to scan packages as well as modules, and call "
"``additional_tests()`` if present to get non-unittest tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8044
msgid ""
"Support namespace packages in conjunction with system packagers, by omitting "
"the installation of any ``__init__.py`` files for namespace packages, and "
"adding a special ``.pth`` file to create a working package in ``sys."
"modules``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8049
msgid ""
"Made ``--single-version-externally-managed`` automatic when ``--root`` is "
"used, so that most system packagers won't require special support for "
"setuptools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8053
msgid ""
"Fixed ``setup_requires``, ``tests_require``, etc. not using ``setup.cfg`` or "
"other configuration files for their option defaults when installing, and "
"also made the install use ``--multi-version`` mode so that the project "
"directory doesn't need to support .pth files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8058
msgid ""
"``MANIFEST.in`` is now forcibly closed when any errors occur while reading "
"it. Previously, the file could be left open and the actual error would be "
"masked by problems trying to remove the open file on Windows systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8062
msgid ""
"Process ``dependency_links.txt`` if found in a distribution, by adding the "
"URLs to the list for scanning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8065
msgid ""
"Use relative paths in ``.pth`` files when eggs are being installed to the "
"same directory as the ``.pth`` file.  This maximizes portability of the "
"target directory when building applications that contain eggs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8069
msgid ""
"Added ``easy_install-N.N`` script(s) for convenience when using multiple "
"Python versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8072
msgid ""
"Added automatic handling of installation conflicts.  Eggs are now shifted to "
"the front of sys.path, in an order consistent with where they came from, "
"making EasyInstall seamlessly co-operate with system package managers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8076
msgid ""
"The ``--delete-conflicting`` and ``--ignore-conflicts-at-my-risk`` options "
"are now no longer necessary, and will generate warnings at the end of a run "
"if you use them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8080
msgid "Don't recursively traverse subdirectories given to ``--find-links``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8083
msgid "0.6a10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8085
msgid "Fixed the ``develop`` command ignoring ``--find-links``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8087
msgid ""
"Added exhaustive testing of the install directory, including a spawn test "
"for ``.pth`` file support, and directory writability/existence checks.  This "
"should virtually eliminate the need to set or configure ``--site-dirs``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8091
msgid ""
"Added ``--prefix`` option for more do-what-I-mean-ishness in the absence of "
"RTFM-ing.  :)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8094
msgid ""
"Enhanced ``PYTHONPATH`` support so that you don't have to put any eggs on it "
"manually to make it work.  ``--multi-version`` is no longer a silent "
"default; you must explicitly use it if installing to a non-PYTHONPATH, non-"
"\"site\" directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8099
msgid ""
"Expand ``$variables`` used in the ``--site-dirs``, ``--build-directory``, "
"``--install-dir``, and ``--script-dir`` options, whether on the command line "
"or in configuration files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8103
msgid ""
"Improved SourceForge mirror processing to work faster and be less affected "
"by transient HTML changes made by SourceForge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8106
msgid ""
"PyPI searches now use the exact spelling of requirements specified on the "
"command line or in a project's ``install_requires``.  Previously, a "
"normalized form of the name was used, which could lead to unnecessary full-"
"index searches when a project's name had an underscore (``_``) in it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8111
msgid ""
"EasyInstall can now download bare ``.py`` files and wrap them in an egg, as "
"long as you include an ``#egg=name-version`` suffix on the URL, or if the ``."
"py`` file is listed as the \"Download URL\" on the project's PyPI page. This "
"allows third parties to \"package\" trivial Python modules just by linking "
"to them (e.g. from within their own PyPI page or download links page)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8118
msgid ""
"The ``--always-copy`` option now skips \"system\" and \"development\" eggs "
"since they can't be reliably copied.  Note that this may cause EasyInstall "
"to choose an older version of a package than what you expected, or it may "
"cause downloading and installation of a fresh version of what's already "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8123
msgid ""
"The ``--find-links`` option previously scanned all supplied URLs and "
"directories as early as possible, but now only directories and direct "
"archive links are scanned immediately.  URLs are not retrieved unless a "
"package search was already going to go online due to a package not being "
"available locally, or due to the use of the ``--update`` or ``-U`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8129
msgid "Fixed the annoying ``--help-commands`` wart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8132
msgid "0.6a9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8134
msgid ""
"The ``sdist`` command no longer uses the traditional ``MANIFEST`` file to "
"create source distributions.  ``MANIFEST.in`` is still read and processed, "
"as are the standard defaults and pruning. But the manifest is built inside "
"the project's ``.egg-info`` directory as ``SOURCES.txt``, and it is rebuilt "
"every time the ``egg_info`` command is run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8140
msgid ""
"Added the ``include_package_data`` keyword to ``setup()``, allowing you to "
"automatically include any package data listed in revision control or "
"``MANIFEST.in``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8144
msgid ""
"Added the ``exclude_package_data`` keyword to ``setup()``, allowing you to "
"trim back files included via the ``package_data`` and "
"``include_package_data`` options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8148
msgid ""
"Fixed ``--tag-svn-revision`` not working when run from a source distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8151
msgid ""
"Added warning for namespace packages with missing ``declare_namespace()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8153
msgid ""
"Added ``tests_require`` keyword to ``setup()``, so that e.g. packages "
"requiring ``nose`` to run unit tests can make this dependency optional "
"unless the ``test`` command is run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8157
msgid ""
"Made all commands that use ``easy_install`` respect its configuration "
"options, as this was causing some problems with ``setup.py install``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8160
msgid ""
"Added an ``unpack_directory()`` driver to ``setuptools.archive_util``, so "
"that you can process a directory tree through a processing filter as if it "
"were a zipfile or tarfile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8164
msgid ""
"Added an internal ``install_egg_info`` command to use as part of old-style "
"``install`` operations, that installs an ``.egg-info`` directory with the "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8168
msgid ""
"Added a ``--single-version-externally-managed`` option to the ``install`` "
"command so that you can more easily wrap a \"flat\" egg in a system package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8171
msgid ""
"Enhanced ``bdist_rpm`` so that it installs single-version eggs that don't "
"rely on a ``.pth`` file. The ``--no-egg`` option has been removed, since all "
"RPMs are now built in a more backwards-compatible format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8175
msgid ""
"Support full roundtrip translation of eggs to and from ``bdist_wininst`` "
"format. Running ``bdist_wininst`` on a setuptools-based package wraps the "
"egg in an .exe that will safely install it as an egg (i.e., with metadata "
"and entry-point wrapper scripts), and ``easy_install`` can turn the .exe "
"back into an ``.egg`` file or directory and install it as such."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8181
msgid ""
"Fixed ``.pth`` file processing picking up nested eggs (i.e. ones inside "
"\"baskets\") when they weren't explicitly listed in the ``.pth`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8184
msgid ""
"If more than one URL appears to describe the exact same distribution, prefer "
"the shortest one.  This helps to avoid \"table of contents\" CGI URLs like "
"the ones on effbot.org."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8188
msgid ""
"Quote arguments to python.exe (including python's path) to avoid problems "
"when Python (or a script) is installed in a directory whose name contains "
"spaces on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8192
msgid ""
"Support full roundtrip translation of eggs to and from ``bdist_wininst`` "
"format.  Running ``bdist_wininst`` on a setuptools-based package wraps the "
"egg in an .exe that will safely install it as an egg (i.e., with metadata "
"and entry-point wrapper scripts), and ``easy_install`` can turn the .exe "
"back into an ``.egg`` file or directory and install it as such."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8199
msgid "0.6a8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8201 (links).rst:8235
msgid ""
"Fixed some problems building extensions when Pyrex was installed, especially "
"with Python 2.4 and/or packages using SWIG."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8204
msgid ""
"Made ``develop`` command accept all the same options as ``easy_install``, "
"and use the ``easy_install`` command's configuration settings as defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8207
msgid ""
"Made ``egg_info --tag-svn-revision`` fall back to extracting the revision "
"number from ``PKG-INFO`` in case it is being run on a source distribution of "
"a snapshot taken from a Subversion-based project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8211
msgid ""
"Automatically detect ``.dll``, ``.so`` and ``.dylib`` files that are being "
"installed as data, adding them to ``native_libs.txt`` automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8214
msgid ""
"Fixed some problems with fresh checkouts of projects that don't include ``."
"egg-info/PKG-INFO`` under revision control and put the project's source code "
"directly in the project directory. If such a package had any requirements "
"that get processed before the ``egg_info`` command can be run, the setup "
"scripts would fail with a \"Missing 'Version:' header and/or PKG-INFO file\" "
"error, because the egg runtime interpreted the unbuilt metadata in a "
"directory on ``sys.path`` (i.e. the current directory) as being a corrupted "
"egg. Setuptools now monkeypatches the distribution metadata cache to pretend "
"that the egg has valid version information, until it has a chance to make it "
"actually be so (via the ``egg_info`` command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8225
msgid "Update for changed SourceForge mirror format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8227
msgid ""
"Fixed not installing dependencies for some packages fetched via Subversion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8229
msgid ""
"Fixed dependency installation with ``--always-copy`` not using the same "
"dependency resolution procedure as other operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8232
msgid ""
"Fixed not fully removing temporary directories on Windows, if a Subversion "
"checkout left read-only files behind"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8239
msgid "0.6a7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8241
msgid ""
"Fixed not being able to install Windows script wrappers using Python 2.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8244
msgid "0.6a6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8246
msgid ""
"Added support for \"traditional\" PYTHONPATH-based non-root installation, "
"and also the convenient ``virtual-python.py`` script, based on a "
"contribution by Ian Bicking.  The setuptools egg now contains a hacked "
"``site`` module that makes the PYTHONPATH-based approach work with .pth "
"files, so that you can get the full EasyInstall feature set on such "
"installations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8252
msgid "Added ``--no-deps`` and ``--allow-hosts`` options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8254
msgid ""
"Improved Windows ``.exe`` script wrappers so that the script can have the "
"same name as a module without confusing Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8257
msgid ""
"Changed dependency processing so that it's breadth-first, allowing a "
"depender's preferences to override those of a dependee, to prevent conflicts "
"when a lower version is acceptable to the dependee, but not the depender. "
"Also, ensure that currently installed/selected packages aren't given "
"precedence over ones desired by a package being installed, which could cause "
"conflict errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8265
msgid "0.6a5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8267
msgid "Fixed missing gui/cli .exe files in distribution. Fixed bugs in tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8270
msgid "0.6a3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8272
msgid ""
"Added ``gui_scripts`` entry point group to allow installing GUI scripts on "
"Windows and other platforms.  (The special handling is only for Windows; "
"other platforms are treated the same as for ``console_scripts``.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8276
msgid ""
"Improved error message when trying to use old ways of running "
"``easy_install``.  Removed the ability to run via ``python -m`` or by "
"running ``easy_install.py``; ``easy_install`` is the command to run on all "
"supported platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8281
msgid ""
"Improved wrapper script generation and runtime initialization so that a "
"VersionConflict doesn't occur if you later install a competing version of a "
"needed package as the default version of that package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8285
msgid "Fixed a problem parsing version numbers in ``#egg=`` links."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8288
msgid "0.6a2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8290
msgid ""
"Added ``console_scripts`` entry point group to allow installing scripts "
"without the need to create separate script files. On Windows, console "
"scripts get an ``.exe`` wrapper so you can just type their name. On other "
"platforms, the scripts are written without a file extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8295
msgid ""
"EasyInstall can now install \"console_scripts\" defined by packages that use "
"``setuptools`` and define appropriate entry points.  On Windows, console "
"scripts get an ``.exe`` wrapper so you can just type their name.  On other "
"platforms, the scripts are installed without a file extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8300
msgid ""
"Using ``python -m easy_install`` or running ``easy_install.py`` is now "
"DEPRECATED, since an ``easy_install`` wrapper is now available on all "
"platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8305
msgid "0.6a1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8307
msgid ""
"Added support for building \"old-style\" RPMs that don't install an egg for "
"the target package, using a ``--no-egg`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8310
msgid ""
"The ``build_ext`` command now works better when using the ``--inplace`` "
"option and multiple Python versions. It now makes sure that all extensions "
"match the current Python version, even if newer copies were built for a "
"different Python version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8315
msgid ""
"The ``upload`` command no longer attaches an extra ``.zip`` when uploading "
"eggs, as PyPI now supports egg uploads without trickery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8318
msgid ""
"The ``ez_setup`` script/module now displays a warning before downloading the "
"setuptools egg, and attempts to check the downloaded egg against an internal "
"MD5 checksum table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8322
msgid ""
"Fixed the ``--tag-svn-revision`` option of ``egg_info`` not finding the "
"latest revision number; it was using the revision number of the directory "
"containing ``setup.py``, not the highest revision number in the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8326
msgid "Added ``eager_resources`` setup argument"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8328
msgid ""
"The ``sdist`` command now recognizes Subversion \"deleted file\" entries and "
"does not include them in source distributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8331
msgid ""
"``setuptools`` now embeds itself more thoroughly into the distutils, so that "
"other distutils extensions (e.g. py2exe, py2app) will subclass setuptools' "
"versions of things, rather than the native distutils ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8335
msgid ""
"Added ``entry_points`` and ``setup_requires`` arguments to ``setup()``; "
"``setup_requires`` allows you to automatically find and download packages "
"that are needed in order to *build* your project (as opposed to running it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8339
msgid ""
"``setuptools`` now finds its commands, ``setup()`` argument validators, and "
"metadata writers using entry points, so that they can be extended by third-"
"party packages. See `Creating distutils Extensions <https://setuptools.pypa."
"io/en/latest/setuptools.html#creating-distutils-extensions>`_ for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8345
msgid ""
"The vestigial ``depends`` command has been removed. It was never finished or "
"documented, and never would have worked without EasyInstall - which it pre-"
"dated and was never compatible with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8349
msgid ""
"EasyInstall now does MD5 validation of downloads from PyPI, or from any link "
"that has an \"#md5=...\" trailer with a 32-digit lowercase hex md5 digest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8352
msgid ""
"EasyInstall now handles symlinks in target directories by removing the link, "
"rather than attempting to overwrite the link's destination.  This makes it "
"easier to set up an alternate Python \"home\" directory (as described in the "
"Non-Root Installation section of the docs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8357
msgid ""
"Added support for handling MacOS platform information in ``.egg`` filenames, "
"based on a contribution by Kevin Dangoor.  You may wish to delete and "
"reinstall any eggs whose filename includes \"darwin\" and "
"\"Power_Macintosh\", because the format for this platform information has "
"changed so that minor OS X upgrades (such as 10.4.1 to 10.4.2) do not cause "
"eggs built with a previous OS version to become obsolete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8364
msgid ""
"easy_install's dependency processing algorithms have changed.  When using "
"``--always-copy``, it now ensures that dependencies are copied too.  When "
"not using ``--always-copy``, it tries to use a single resolution loop, "
"rather than recursing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8369
msgid ""
"Fixed installing extra ``.pyc`` or ``.pyo`` files for scripts with ``.py`` "
"extensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8372
msgid ""
"Added ``--site-dirs`` option to allow adding custom \"site\" directories. "
"Made ``easy-install.pth`` work in platform-specific alternate site "
"directories (e.g. ``~/Library/Python/2.x/site-packages`` on Mac OS X)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8376
msgid ""
"If you manually delete the current version of a package, the next run of "
"EasyInstall against the target directory will now remove the stray entry "
"from the ``easy-install.pth`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8380
msgid ""
"EasyInstall now recognizes URLs with a ``#egg=project_name`` fragment ID as "
"pointing to the named project's source checkout.  Such URLs have a lower "
"match precedence than any other kind of distribution, so they'll only be "
"used if they have a higher version number than any other available "
"distribution, or if you use the ``--editable`` option.  The ``#egg`` "
"fragment can contain a version if it's formatted as ``#egg=proj-ver``, where "
"``proj`` is the project name, and ``ver`` is the version number.  You *must* "
"use the format for these values that the ``bdist_egg`` command uses; i.e., "
"all non-alphanumeric runs must be condensed to single underscore characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8391
msgid ""
"Added the ``--editable`` option; see Editing and Viewing Source Packages in "
"the docs.  Also, slightly changed the behavior of the ``--build-directory`` "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8395
msgid ""
"Fixed the setup script sandbox facility not recognizing certain paths as "
"valid on case-insensitive platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8399
msgid "0.5a12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8401
msgid ""
"The zip-safety scanner now checks for modules that might be used with "
"``python -m``, and marks them as unsafe for zipping, since Python 2.4 can't "
"handle ``-m`` on zipped modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8405
msgid ""
"Fix ``python -m easy_install`` not working due to setuptools being installed "
"as a zipfile.  Update safety scanner to check for modules that might be used "
"as ``python -m`` scripts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8409
msgid ""
"Misc. fixes for win32.exe support, including changes to support Python 2.4's "
"changed ``bdist_wininst`` format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8413
msgid "0.5a11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8415
msgid ""
"Fix breakage of the \"develop\" command that was caused by the addition of "
"``--always-unzip`` to the ``easy_install`` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8419
msgid "0.5a10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8421
msgid ""
"Put the ``easy_install`` module back in as a module, as it's needed for "
"``python -m`` to run it!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8424
msgid ""
"Allow ``--find-links/-f`` to accept local directories or filenames as well "
"as URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8428
msgid "0.5a9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8430
msgid ""
"Include ``svn:externals`` directories in source distributions as well as "
"normal subversion-controlled files and directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8433
msgid "Added ``exclude=patternlist`` option to ``setuptools.find_packages()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8435
msgid ""
"Changed --tag-svn-revision to include an \"r\" in front of the revision "
"number for better readability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8438
msgid ""
"Added ability to build eggs without including source files (except for any "
"scripts, of course), using the ``--exclude-source-files`` option to "
"``bdist_egg``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8442
msgid ""
"``setup.py install`` now automatically detects when an \"unmanaged\" package "
"or module is going to be on ``sys.path`` ahead of a package being installed, "
"thereby preventing the newer version from being imported. If this occurs, a "
"warning message is output to ``sys.stderr``, but installation proceeds "
"anyway. The warning message informs the user what files or directories need "
"deleting, and advises them they can also use EasyInstall (with the ``--"
"delete-conflicting`` option) to do it automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8450
msgid ""
"The ``egg_info`` command now adds a ``top_level.txt`` file to the metadata "
"directory that lists all top-level modules and packages in the distribution. "
"This is used by the ``easy_install`` command to find possibly-conflicting "
"\"unmanaged\" packages when installing the distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8455
msgid ""
"Added ``zip_safe`` and ``namespace_packages`` arguments to ``setup()``. "
"Added package analysis to determine zip-safety if the ``zip_safe`` flag is "
"not given, and advise the author regarding what code might need changing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8459
msgid "Fixed the swapped ``-d`` and ``-b`` options of ``bdist_egg``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8461
msgid ""
"EasyInstall now automatically detects when an \"unmanaged\" package or "
"module is going to be on ``sys.path`` ahead of a package you're installing, "
"thereby preventing the newer version from being imported.  By default, it "
"will abort installation to alert you of the problem, but there are also new "
"options (``--delete-conflicting`` and ``--ignore-conflicts-at-my-risk``) "
"available to change the default behavior.  (Note: this new feature doesn't "
"take effect for egg files that were built with older ``setuptools`` "
"versions, because they lack the new metadata file required to implement it.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8470
msgid ""
"The ``easy_install`` distutils command now uses ``DistutilsError`` as its "
"base error type for errors that should just issue a message to stderr and "
"exit the program without a traceback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8474
msgid ""
"EasyInstall can now be given a path to a directory containing a setup "
"script, and it will attempt to build and install the package there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8477
msgid ""
"EasyInstall now performs a safety analysis on module contents to determine "
"whether a package is likely to run in zipped form, and displays information "
"about what modules may be doing introspection that would break when running "
"as a zipfile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8482
msgid ""
"Added the ``--always-unzip/-Z`` option, to force unzipping of packages that "
"would ordinarily be considered safe to unzip, and changed the meaning of ``--"
"zip-ok/-z`` to \"always leave everything zipped\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8487
msgid "0.5a8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8489
msgid ""
"The \"egg_info\" command now always sets the distribution metadata to "
"\"safe\" forms of the distribution name and version, so that distribution "
"files will be generated with parseable names (i.e., ones that don't include "
"'-' in the name or version). Also, this means that if you use the various "
"``--tag`` options of \"egg_info\", any distributions generated will use the "
"tags in the version, not just egg distributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8496
msgid ""
"Added support for defining command aliases in distutils configuration files, "
"under the \"[aliases]\" section. To prevent recursion and to allow aliases "
"to call the command of the same name, a given alias can be expanded only "
"once per command-line invocation. You can define new aliases with the "
"\"alias\" command, either for the local, global, or per-user configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8502
msgid ""
"Added \"rotate\" command to delete old distribution files, given a set of "
"patterns to match and the number of files to keep.  (Keeps the most recently-"
"modified distribution files matching each pattern.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8506
msgid ""
"Added \"saveopts\" command that saves all command-line options for the "
"current invocation to the local, global, or per-user configuration file. "
"Useful for setting defaults without having to hand-edit a configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8510
msgid ""
"Added a \"setopt\" command that sets a single option in a specified "
"distutils configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8513
msgid ""
"There is now a separate documentation page for setuptools; revision history "
"that's not specific to EasyInstall has been moved to that page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8517
msgid "0.5a7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8519
msgid ""
"Added \"upload\" support for egg and source distributions, including a bug "
"fix for \"upload\" and a temporary workaround for lack of .egg support in "
"PyPI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8524
msgid "0.5a6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8526
msgid ""
"Beefed up the \"sdist\" command so that if you don't have a MANIFEST.in, it "
"will include all files under revision control (CVS or Subversion) in the "
"current directory, and it will regenerate the list every time you create a "
"source distribution, not just when you tell it to. This should make the "
"default \"do what you mean\" more often than the distutils' default behavior "
"did, while still retaining the old behavior in the presence of MANIFEST.in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8533
msgid ""
"Fixed the \"develop\" command always updating .pth files, even if you "
"specified ``-n`` or ``--dry-run``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8536
msgid ""
"Slightly changed the format of the generated version when you use ``--tag-"
"build`` on the \"egg_info\" command, so that you can make tagged revisions "
"compare *lower* than the version specified in setup.py (e.g. by using ``--"
"tag-build=dev``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8542
msgid "0.5a5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8544
msgid ""
"Added ``develop`` command to ``setuptools``-based packages. This command "
"installs an ``.egg-link`` pointing to the package's source directory, and "
"script wrappers that ``execfile()`` the source versions of the package's "
"scripts. This lets you put your development checkout(s) on sys.path without "
"having to actually install them.  (To uninstall the link, use use ``setup.py "
"develop --uninstall``.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8551
msgid ""
"Added ``egg_info`` command to ``setuptools``-based packages. This command "
"just creates or updates the \"projectname.egg-info\" directory, without "
"building an egg.  (It's used by the ``bdist_egg``, ``test``, and ``develop`` "
"commands.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8556
msgid ""
"Enhanced the ``test`` command so that it doesn't install the package, but "
"instead builds any C extensions in-place, updates the ``.egg-info`` "
"metadata, adds the source directory to ``sys.path``, and runs the tests "
"directly on the source. This avoids an \"unmanaged\" installation of the "
"package to ``site-packages`` or elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8562
msgid ""
"Made ``easy_install`` a standard ``setuptools`` command, moving it from the "
"``easy_install`` module to ``setuptools.command.easy_install``. Note that if "
"you were importing or extending it, you must now change your imports "
"accordingly.  ``easy_install.py`` is still installed as a script, but not as "
"a module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8569
msgid "0.5a4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8571
msgid ""
"Setup scripts using setuptools can now list their dependencies directly in "
"the setup.py file, without having to manually create a ``depends.txt`` file. "
"The ``install_requires`` and ``extras_require`` arguments to ``setup()`` are "
"used to create a dependencies file automatically. If you are manually "
"creating ``depends.txt`` right now, please switch to using these setup "
"arguments as soon as practical, because ``depends.txt`` support will be "
"removed in the 0.6 release cycle. For documentation on the new arguments, "
"see the ``setuptools.dist.Distribution`` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8580
msgid ""
"Setup scripts using setuptools now always install using ``easy_install`` "
"internally, for ease of uninstallation and upgrading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8583
msgid ""
"Added ``--always-copy/-a`` option to always copy needed packages to the "
"installation directory, even if they're already present elsewhere on sys."
"path. (In previous versions, this was the default behavior, but now you must "
"request it.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8588
msgid ""
"Added ``--upgrade/-U`` option to force checking PyPI for latest available "
"version(s) of all packages requested by name and version, even if a matching "
"version is available locally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8592
msgid ""
"Added automatic installation of dependencies declared by a distribution "
"being installed.  These dependencies must be listed in the distribution's "
"``EGG-INFO`` directory, so the distribution has to have declared its "
"dependencies by using setuptools.  If a package has requirements it didn't "
"declare, you'll still have to deal with them yourself.  (E.g., by asking "
"EasyInstall to find and install them.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8599
msgid ""
"Added the ``--record`` option to ``easy_install`` for the benefit of tools "
"that run ``setup.py install --record=filename`` on behalf of another "
"packaging system.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8604
msgid "0.5a3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8606
msgid "Fixed not setting script permissions to allow execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8608
msgid ""
"Improved sandboxing so that setup scripts that want a temporary directory (e."
"g. pychecker) can still run in the sandbox."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8612
msgid "0.5a2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8614
msgid "Fix stupid stupid refactoring-at-the-last-minute typos.  :("
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8617
msgid "0.5a1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8619
msgid ""
"Added support for \"self-installation\" bootstrapping. Packages can now "
"include ``ez_setup.py`` in their source distribution, and add the following "
"to their ``setup.py``, in order to automatically bootstrap installation of "
"setuptools as part of their setup process::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8624
msgid ""
"from ez_setup import use_setuptools\n"
"use_setuptools()\n"
"\n"
"from setuptools import setup\n"
"# etc..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8630
msgid ""
"Added support for converting ``.win32.exe`` installers to eggs on the fly. "
"EasyInstall will now recognize such files by name and install them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8633
msgid ""
"Fixed a problem with picking the \"best\" version to install (versions were "
"being sorted as strings, rather than as parsed values)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8637
msgid "0.4a4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8639
msgid ""
"Added support for the distutils \"verbose/quiet\" and \"dry-run\" options, "
"as well as the \"optimize\" flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8642
msgid ""
"Support downloading packages that were uploaded to PyPI (by scanning all "
"links on package pages, not just the homepage/download links)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8646
msgid "0.4a3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8648
msgid ""
"Add progress messages to the search/download process so that you can tell "
"what URLs it's reading to find download links.  (Hopefully, this will help "
"people report out-of-date and broken links to package authors, and to tell "
"when they've asked for a package that doesn't exist.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8654
msgid "0.4a2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8656
msgid ""
"Added ``ez_setup.py`` installer/bootstrap script to make initial setuptools "
"installation easier, and to allow distributions using setuptools to avoid "
"having to include setuptools in their source distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8660
msgid ""
"All downloads are now managed by the ``PackageIndex`` class (which is now "
"subclassable and replaceable), so that embedders can more easily override "
"download logic, give download progress reports, etc. The class has also been "
"moved to the new ``setuptools.package_index`` module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8665
msgid ""
"The ``Installer`` class no longer handles downloading, manages a temporary "
"directory, or tracks the ``zip_ok`` option. Downloading is now handled by "
"``PackageIndex``, and ``Installer`` has become an ``easy_install`` command "
"class based on ``setuptools.Command``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8670
msgid ""
"There is a new ``setuptools.sandbox.run_setup()`` API to invoke a setup "
"script in a directory sandbox, and a new ``setuptools.archive_util`` module "
"with an ``unpack_archive()`` API. These were split out of EasyInstall to "
"allow reuse by other tools and applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8675
msgid ""
"``setuptools.Command`` now supports reinitializing commands using keyword "
"arguments to set/reset options. Also, ``Command`` subclasses can now set "
"their ``command_consumes_arguments`` attribute to ``True`` in order to "
"receive an ``args`` option containing the rest of the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8680
msgid "Added support for installing scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8682
msgid ""
"Added support for setting options via distutils configuration files, and "
"using distutils' default options as a basis for EasyInstall's defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8685
msgid ""
"Renamed ``--scan-url/-s`` to ``--find-links/-f`` to free up ``-s`` for the "
"script installation directory option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8688
msgid ""
"Use ``urllib2`` instead of ``urllib``, to allow use of ``https:`` URLs if "
"Python includes SSL support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8692
msgid "0.4a1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8694
msgid ""
"Added ``--scan-url`` and ``--index-url`` options, to scan download pages and "
"search PyPI for needed packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8698
msgid "0.3a4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8700
msgid ""
"Restrict ``--build-directory=DIR/-b DIR`` option to only be used with single "
"URL installs, to avoid running the wrong setup.py."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8704
msgid "0.3a3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8706
msgid "Added ``--build-directory=DIR/-b DIR`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8708
msgid ""
"Added \"installation report\" that explains how to use 'require()' when "
"doing a multiversion install or alternate installation directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8711
msgid "Added SourceForge mirror auto-select (Contributed by Ian Bicking)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8713
msgid ""
"Added \"sandboxing\" that stops a setup script from running if it attempts "
"to write to the filesystem outside of the build area"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8716
msgid "Added more workarounds for packages with quirky ``install_data`` hacks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8719
msgid "0.3a2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8721
msgid ""
"Added new options to ``bdist_egg`` to allow tagging the egg's version number "
"with a subversion revision number, the current date, or an explicit tag "
"value. Run ``setup.py bdist_egg --help`` to get more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8725
msgid ""
"Added subversion download support for ``svn:`` and ``svn+`` URLs, as well as "
"automatic recognition of HTTP subversion URLs (Contributed by Ian Bicking)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8728
msgid "Misc. bug fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8731
msgid "0.3a1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../NEWS (links).rst:8733
msgid "Initial release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../history.rst:16
msgid "Credits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../history.rst:18
msgid ""
"The original design for the ``.egg`` format and the ``pkg_resources`` API "
"was co-created by Phillip Eby and Bob Ippolito. Bob also implemented the "
"first version of ``pkg_resources``, and supplied the macOS operating system "
"version compatibility algorithm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../history.rst:23
msgid ""
"Ian Bicking implemented many early \"creature comfort\" features of "
"easy_install, including support for downloading via Sourceforge and "
"Subversion repositories. Ian's comments on the Web-SIG about WSGI "
"application deployment also inspired the concept of \"entry points\" in "
"eggs, and he has given talks at PyCon and elsewhere to inform and educate "
"the community about eggs and setuptools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../history.rst:30
msgid ""
"Jim Fulton contributed time and effort to build automated tests of various "
"aspects of ``easy_install``, and supplied the doctests for the command-line "
"``.exe`` wrappers on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../history.rst:34
msgid ""
"Phillip J. Eby is the seminal author of setuptools, and first proposed the "
"idea of an importable binary distribution format for Python application plug-"
"ins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../history.rst:38
msgid ""
"Significant parts of the implementation of setuptools were funded by the "
"Open Source Applications Foundation, to provide a plug-in infrastructure for "
"the Chandler PIM application. In addition, many OSAF staffers (such as Mike "
"\"Code Bear\" Taylor) contributed their time and stress as guinea pigs for "
"the use of eggs and setuptools, even before eggs were \"cool\".  (Thanks, "
"guys!)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../history.rst:44
msgid ""
"Tarek Ziadé is the principal author of the Distribute fork, which re-"
"invigorated the community on the project, encouraged renewed innovation, and "
"addressed many defects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../history.rst:48
msgid ""
"Jason R. Coombs performed the merge with Distribute, maintaining the project "
"for several years in coordination with the Python Packaging Authority (PyPA)."
msgstr ""
